{
  "about": "Contributions every client resolves the same way (D17, D19): `menu/*` items for a place (visible: owner on, or allowed in safe mode, and command available or client.*; `when` matched field by field; sorted by order then id) and key winners (highest priority, then client defaults, then lowest id; keys that don't parse are ignored; client.none unbinds). `menus` maps place -> [entry id], `keys` maps canonical key -> winning binding id (`builtin:<key>` for client defaults) or null when unbound, `gestures` maps `<key> <where>` -> binding id. Generated by the Rust model (tests/client_conformance.rs, VQRO_FIXTURE_UPDATE=1) and reviewed. Scoped keys (D29): `scoped` lists [key, scope, ctx] queries -> the winning binding's command (or null): scope \"pane\" (no prefix, not typing) or \"composer\" (while typing); `when` matched against ctx; never in terminal panes; prefix-scoped bindings are not candidates and scoped ones never appear among prefix keys.",
